# Supabase project credentials
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# NOTE: GEMINI_API_KEY is NOT a frontend variable and must never be added here.
# It is read inside the Edge Function via Deno.env.get("GEMINI_API_KEY")
# (supabase/functions/analyze-resumes/index.ts), so store it as a Supabase secret:
#   Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Edge Functions -> Secrets
#   or: supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# The function also needs:
#   - the `cv_analyses` table (supabase/migrations/20260923_create_cv_analyses_table.sql)
#   - to be deployed as `analyze-resumes` with JWT verification disabled,
#     because this app has no login and sends no Authorization header.
#
# OPTIONAL secret: GEMINI_MODEL overrides the default model (gemini-3.6-flash),
# so you can switch models after a deprecation without redeploying the function.
